# Story: someone has the editor framed on the laptop and is typing in a terminal on the big display. The cable comes out
# in the middle of a sentence. The rest of the sentence must go into a window they can see; and the same when the
# cable goes in again. (The product owner: a change of displays ends with the focused window in view, as a resume does.)
# Spec: docs/features/F08-displays-and-spaces.md. Window ids start at 101.
quiet
displays 2
open Code
open Safari
open Terminal
move 103 1600 100 600 400
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
zoom 101
wait 5
focus 103
type
loud
# The cable comes out. The terminal floats on the laptop now, whose view was on the editor alone.
displays 1
wait 3
expect visible 103
expect ring 103
type
# Back at the desk. It goes home, and is in view there as well.
displays 2
wait 3
expect visible 103
expect ring 103
# The laptop's view is where the keyboard took it. Back is the way to the editor.
cursor 700 400
back
expect visible 101
